task: intent-split-other
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-split-other
worktree: ../okay-wt-split

why: the worst measured property of what this module SHIPS. `Other`
  scores recall 0.47 in the shipped composite — more than half the
  messages that are not about meetings get routed INTO a meeting
  intent, which in production is the failure that reaches a person.

what is already known, so this does not repeat it:
  - `Other` is ONE incoherent cloud, not two clusters (mean pairwise
    cosine within pleasantries 0.645, within complaints 0.560, across
    0.551 — every real class is tighter than anything inside it).
  - Rejection-by-threshold is TWENTY POINTS WORSE (68.3% against
    88.3%): an incoherent bin can still be learned when its members
    are individually distinctive, and a floor throws that away.
  - The option left open by intent-other-is-a-bin is the one here:
    split it into NAMED classes that are individually coherent.

what: a derived 5-class view (Social, Support beside the three meeting
  classes) measured against the 4-class canon, on the same rows and
  the same tiers. The fixture's canonical labels are NOT changed —
  every published number stays comparable — and the decision to ship
  a 5-class model comes after the measurement, not with it.

the number that decides it: UNION RECALL. Of the held-out messages
  that are not about meetings, how many land in a non-meeting class at
  all. 0.47 is the bar.

files: okay-intent/src/test/scala/okay/intent/IntentFixture.scala (a
  derived view, not a relabel), a JVM measurement suite,
  specs/intent-classify.md, BACKLOG.md
